IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 9 -- Offences by or relating to public servants`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 161, 162, 163, 164, 165, 166, 167, 168, 169, 170, 171.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- Three families. ss 161 to 165 are GRATIFICATION: the public servant who takes one
-- for an official act (s 161); anyone who takes one to influence a public servant by
-- corrupt or illegal means (s 162) or by personal influence (s 163); the public
-- servant who abets a s 162 or s 163 offence committed in respect of himself
-- (s 164); and the public servant who obtains a valuable thing without adequate
-- consideration from a person concerned in his official business (s 165). ss 166 to
-- 169 are BREACH OF OFFICIAL DUTY: disobeying a direction of the law to injure
-- (s 166), framing an incorrect document to injure (s 167), trading (s 168) and
-- buying property (s 169) when legally bound not to. ss 170 and 171 are PERSONATION:
-- pretending to hold an office (s 170), and wearing the garb of a class of public
-- servants (s 171).
--
-- The s 161 Explanations are definitions carried in the facts rather than as limbs:
-- "gratification" is not restricted to money or things estimable in money; "legal
-- remuneration" includes all remuneration the public servant is permitted by law to
-- accept; and "a motive or reward for doing" reaches one who takes it for what he does
-- not intend to do or has not done. The first Explanation -- a person not expecting
-- office who obtains a gratification by deceiving others into believing he is about
-- to hold it may be cheating but is not within s 161 -- is why `expects to be a
-- public servant` is a fact and not a belief induced in others.
--
-- ss 162 and 163 do not require the taker to be a public servant; the Illustration
-- to s 164 is a public servant's wife. ss 161, 164 to 169 do.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED.

§§ `Section 161 -- Public servant taking a gratification`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 161"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant taking a gratification other than legal remuneration in respect of an official act under Penal Code 1871 section 161
GIVEN ps IS A `Public Servant Offence` @desc A person who is or expects to be a public servant accepting, obtaining, agreeing to accept or attempting to obtain a gratification other than legal remuneration as a motive or reward for an official act, for favour or disfavour in his official functions, or for a service or disservice with the Government, a Member or a public servant.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant taking a gratification` IF
        (ps's `is a public servant` OR ps's `expects to be a public servant`)
    AND ps's `accepts or obtains or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain from any person for himself or for any other person any gratification whatever`
    AND ps's `the gratification is other than legal remuneration`
    AND ps's `as a motive or reward for doing or forbearing to do any official act or for showing or forbearing to show in the exercise of his official functions favour or disfavour to any person or for rendering or attempting to render any service or disservice to any person with the Government or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet or with any public servant as such`

§§ `Sections 162 and 163 -- Taking a gratification to influence a public servant`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 162"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes taking a gratification to influence a public servant by corrupt or illegal means under Penal Code 1871 section 162
GIVEN ps IS A `Public Servant Offence` @desc Accepting, obtaining, agreeing to accept or attempting to obtain a gratification as a motive or reward for inducing, by corrupt or illegal means, a public servant to act or forbear, show favour or disfavour, or render a service or disservice. The taker need not be a public servant.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes taking a gratification to corruptly influence a public servant` IF
        ps's `accepts or obtains or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain from any person for himself or for any other person any gratification whatever`
    AND ps's `as a motive or reward for inducing by corrupt or illegal means any public servant to do or forbear to do any official act or in the exercise of his official functions to show favour or disfavour to any person or to render or attempt to render any service or disservice to any person with the Government or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet or with any public servant as such`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 163"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes taking a gratification for the exercise of personal influence with a public servant under Penal Code 1871 section 163
GIVEN ps IS A `Public Servant Offence` @desc The same taking, as a motive or reward for inducing a public servant by the exercise of personal influence. The Illustration excludes an advocate's fee, a paid memorialist and a paid agent laying statements before the Government: none exercises or professes to exercise personal influence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes taking a gratification for personal influence with a public servant` IF
        ps's `accepts or obtains or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain from any person for himself or for any other person any gratification whatever`
    AND ps's `as a motive or reward for inducing by the exercise of personal influence any public servant to do or forbear to do any official act or in the exercise of his official functions to show favour or disfavour to any person or to render or attempt to render any service or disservice to any person with the Government or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet or with any public servant as such`

§§ `Section 164 -- Abetment by the public servant concerned`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 164"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant abetting a section 162 or 163 offence committed in respect of himself under Penal Code 1871 section 164
GIVEN ps IS A `Public Servant Offence` @desc A public servant in respect of whom a s 162 or s 163 offence is committed, who abets it. The Illustration: a public servant abetting his wife's taking of a present to solicit him for an office.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant abetting the taking of a gratification to influence him` IF
        ps's `is a public servant`
    AND ps's `is the public servant in respect of whom an offence under section 162 or 163 is committed`
    AND ps's `abets that offence`

§§ `Section 165 -- Valuable thing without consideration`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 165"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant obtaining a valuable thing without consideration from a person concerned in his official business under Penal Code 1871 section 165
GIVEN ps IS A `Public Servant Offence` @desc A public servant accepting, obtaining, agreeing to accept or attempting to obtain a valuable thing without consideration or for one he knows to be inadequate, from a person he knows to be concerned in proceedings or business transacted by him or connected with his or his superior's official functions, or from a person he knows to be interested in or related to such a person. The Illustrations are a judge renting below market from a litigant, buying notes at a discount from one, and selling shares at a premium to one's brother.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant obtaining a valuable thing without consideration` IF
        ps's `is a public servant`
    AND ps's `accepts or obtains or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain for himself or for any other person any valuable thing without consideration or for a consideration which he knows to be inadequate`
    AND ps's `from a person whom he knows to have been or to be or to be likely to be concerned in any proceedings or business transacted or about to be transacted by him or having any connection with his official functions or those of any public servant to whom he is subordinate or from a person whom he knows to be interested in or related to the person so concerned`

§§ `Sections 166 and 167 -- Disobeying the law, and framing an incorrect document, to cause injury`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 166"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant disobeying a direction of the law with intent to cause injury under Penal Code 1871 section 166
GIVEN ps IS A `Public Servant Offence` @desc A public servant knowingly disobeying a direction of the law as to how he is to conduct himself as such, intending to cause or knowing it likely that he will cause injury to any person. The Illustration is an enforcement officer who knowingly disobeys the direction to take property under an enforcement order, knowing the judgment creditor is likely to be injured.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant disobeying the law to cause injury` IF
        ps's `is a public servant`
    AND ps's `knowingly disobeys a direction of the law as to the way in which he is to conduct himself as a public servant`
    AND ps's `intends to cause or knows it to be likely that he will by the disobedience cause injury to any person`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 167"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant framing an incorrect document or electronic record with intent to cause injury under Penal Code 1871 section 167
GIVEN ps IS A `Public Servant Offence` @desc A public servant charged with preparing or translating a document or electronic record who frames or translates it in a manner he knows or believes to be incorrect, intending to cause or knowing it likely that he may cause injury to any person.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant framing an incorrect document to cause injury` IF
        ps's `is a public servant`
    AND ps's `is charged as a public servant with the preparation or translation of a document or electronic record`
    AND ps's `frames or translates the document or electronic record in a manner which he knows or believes to be incorrect`
    AND ps's `intends thereby to cause or knows it to be likely that he may thereby cause injury to any person`

§§ `Sections 168 and 169 -- Unlawfully trading, and unlawfully buying property`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 168"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant unlawfully engaging in trade under Penal Code 1871 section 168
GIVEN ps IS A `Public Servant Offence` @desc A public servant legally bound as such not to engage in trade, who engages in trade.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant unlawfully engaging in trade` IF
        ps's `is a public servant`
    AND ps's `is legally bound as a public servant not to engage in trade`
    AND ps's `engages in trade`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 169"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant unlawfully buying or bidding for property under Penal Code 1871 section 169
GIVEN ps IS A `Public Servant Offence` @desc A public servant legally bound as such not to purchase or bid for certain property, who purchases or bids for it in his own name, another's, or jointly or in shares with others. Confiscation of the property is punishment and is not decided.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant unlawfully buying or bidding for property` IF
        ps's `is a public servant`
    AND ps's `is legally bound as a public servant not to purchase or bid for certain property`
    AND ps's `purchases or bids for that property in his own name or in the name of another or jointly or in shares with others`

§§ `Sections 170 and 171 -- Personating a public servant, and wearing his garb`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 170"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes personating a public servant under Penal Code 1871 section 170
GIVEN ps IS A `Public Servant Offence` @desc Pretending to hold a particular office as a public servant knowing he does not, or falsely personating another person holding it, and in that assumed character doing or attempting to do an act under colour of the office.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes personating a public servant` IF
        ps's `pretends to hold a particular office as a public servant knowing that he does not hold it or falsely personates another person holding such office`
    AND ps's `in that assumed character does or attempts to do any act under colour of the office`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 171"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes wearing the garb or carrying the token of a class of public servants with fraudulent intent under Penal Code 1871 section 171
GIVEN ps IS A `Public Servant Offence` @desc A person not belonging to a class of public servants who wears garb or carries a token resembling that class's, intending that it may be believed, or knowing it likely to be believed, that he belongs to the class.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes wearing the garb of a public servant` IF
        ps's `does not belong to a certain class of public servants`
    AND ps's `wears any garb or carries any token resembling any garb or token used by that class of public servants`
    AND ps's `intends that it may be believed or knows it to be likely to be believed that he belongs to that class of public servants`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a gratification offence` IF
        (   `constitutes a public servant taking a gratification` (a's `public servant offence`)
         OR `constitutes taking a gratification to corruptly influence a public servant` (a's `public servant offence`)
         OR `constitutes taking a gratification for personal influence with a public servant` (a's `public servant offence`)
         OR `constitutes a public servant abetting the taking of a gratification to influence him` (a's `public servant offence`)
         OR `constitutes a public servant obtaining a valuable thing without consideration` (a's `public servant offence`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a breach of official duty` IF
        (   `constitutes a public servant disobeying the law to cause injury` (a's `public servant offence`)
         OR `constitutes a public servant framing an incorrect document to cause injury` (a's `public servant offence`)
         OR `constitutes a public servant unlawfully engaging in trade` (a's `public servant offence`)
         OR `constitutes a public servant unlawfully buying or bidding for property` (a's `public servant offence`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes personating a public servant` IF
        (   `constitutes personating a public servant` (a's `public servant offence`)
         OR `constitutes wearing the garb of a public servant` (a's `public servant offence`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
